==German==

===Phrase===
'''[[Sitz]] [[im]] [[Leben]]'''

# {{idiom|lang=de}} (sit in life) means at which moment in someones life a kind saying or writing fits.

===Usage notes===
Though often rendered by phrases like "life setting", "situation in life" etc. the German term ''Sitz im Leben'' is usually either translated by "sociological setting" or left untranslated.  As a technical term, it refers to the typical setting of a genre.
While the term isn't necessarily owned by Judeo-Christian theologians, it is a common phrase utilized within the theological perspective of Biblical Criticism.  When the phrase is used in modern dialogue, it is usually within the context of a theological discussion or perspective regarding biblical content or the setting that gives biblical content context within the "life setting" in which it is framed.